{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"CodeGraph emits value-reference edges so impact analysis can catch the “change this constant/table, break its readers” case inside a file, which calls/imports/inheritance alone miss and would otherwise make a value look unused. It keeps them precise by only recording edges when it can resolve the reader confidently, skipping bundled/minified files and ambiguously shadowed names, and it doesn’t add extra nodes to the graph. [CHANGELOG](https://github.com/colbymchenry/codegraph/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md)"}}
